The 1915–16 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 28th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Results for Celtic for 1915-16 |url=https://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1910/celtic1916.htm |website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> Celtic won the League for the third year in a row, by eleven points over nearest rival [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]]. The Scottish Cup was not played for the second consecutive year because of the [[World War I|Great War]].

Celtic won both the [[Glasgow Cup]] and the [[Glasgow Charity Cup|Glasgow Merchants' Charity Cup]].

